feat(app): log a service visit from customer detail

Closes the operations cycle on the customer profile. The detail page
already queried schedule_items and rendered a service-history timeline,
but there was no way to actually CREATE a visit row from the UI — the
timeline was read-only.

- New action logServiceVisit(customerId, type, title, startsAt, notes?)
  in app/(authed)/customers/[id]/actions.ts. Tenant-scoped insert into
  schedule_items with status=completed for past dates and status=
  scheduled for future. Audit-log row written best-effort.
- New LogVisitButton.tsx — opens a dialog with: type radio
  (service / install / warranty / storm_response / inspection), title
  (required), datetime-local picker pre-filled with now in local TZ,
  optional notes textarea. Toast confirms; router.refresh() pulls the
  new row into the timeline.
- Wired into PageHeader actions on /app/customers/[id]. Visible for
  every tenant vertical, not just lighting.

Verification:
- npx tsc --noEmit clean
- npm run lint clean
- npm run build: /app/customers/[id] now 6.59 kB (was 2.22 kB) — diff
  is the dialog + form bundle. Other routes unchanged.

Day-1 onboarding loop is now closed end-to-end:
  TenantOnboardingHero → Add customer (manual or CSV) → /app/customers
  list → /app/customers/[id] detail → Log a visit → service history
  populates → cron picks up units when they age into staleness.
